# trading_analysis_agent

Full-stack research tool for crypto, forex, and metals. Analysis and paper trading only. Do not treat outputs as financial advice.

## Architecture

- `client/`: React + Vite dashboard
- `server/`: Node + Express API and AI agent orchestration (OpenAI)
- `analysis/`: Python FastAPI service for market data, indicators, and backtesting
- Database: Supabase (PostgreSQL)

Keep each concern in its own service. The client talks to the Express API. Express orchestrates the agent and calls the analysis service. Supabase is the system of record.

## Asset classes

Support these classes on one shared path. Do not special-case one so the others cannot use it.

- Crypto pairs, for example `BTC/USDT` and `ETH/USDT`
- Forex pairs, for example `EURUSD` and `GBPJPY`
- Metals, for example Gold (`XAUUSD`, Yahoo `GC=F`) and Silver (`XAGUSD`, Yahoo `SI=F`)

## Market data

Every data source goes through a provider abstraction. Callers depend on the interface, not on a vendor.

Every provider returns the same OHLCV rows:

- `timestamp` — bar open time, UTC
- `open`, `high`, `low`, `close` — prices as decimals
- `volume` — base-asset volume when the source provides it; otherwise null, never a guessed number

Adding a source means a new provider behind that interface. Indicators, backtests, and the agent consume OHLCV only.

## No live trading

No real order execution. No broker order APIs, no exchange trading keys used to place or cancel orders, and no withdrawal flows.

Allowed: market analysis, indicators, backtests, and paper trading (simulated fills recorded locally or in Supabase).

## Secrets

Never hardcode API keys, tokens, connection strings, or other secrets in source, comments, tests, or docs.

- Read secrets from environment variables.
- Each service that needs config gets a `.env` (gitignored) and a committed `.env.example` with placeholder names only.
- Document every new variable in the matching `.env.example`.

```env
# .env.example — names and placeholders only
OPENAI_API_KEY=your_openai_api_key
SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=your_service_role_key
```

## Code

- Keep code clean: small functions, clear names, no unused paths.
- Comment non-obvious intent (why a threshold, timeout, or data transform exists). Do not comment obvious lines.
- Match the language and style already used in the file you are editing.

## UI disclaimer

Any user-facing screen that shows analysis, signals, backtests, or paper trades must include this disclaimer, visible without extra clicks:

Research only, not financial advice.
